{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: repeated repairs silently overwrite the previous backup**

`renamePath(path, '$path.bak')` replaces any existing `.bak`, so a second `fa session repair` destroys the first repair's pristine original with no warning. Since repair is exactly the kind of operation users may run twice (first with `--dry-run`, then for real, then again after realizing a mistake), consider a rotation — e.g. `.bak`, `.bak1`, … — or refusing when a `.bak` already exists unless `--force`.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment4.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: typo in a new public constant name — `ledgetTextCapChars`**

Should be `ledgerTextCapChars` ("ledger", not "ledget"). It's already referenced from three call sites (`shell_job_board.dart`, `subagent_manager.dart`), so the sooner it's renamed the cheaper it is — a public typo tends to get copy-pasted. While here: `_appendSpan` and the `_bytes`/`_formatBytes` helpers are now duplicated between this file and `session_storage.dart` / `session_repair.dart`; worth extracting one shared copy.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment5.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: double newline when quarantining torn lines**

The torn span's `end` already includes the line's trailing `\n` (see `SessionScannedLine.byteLength` — "trailing newline included"), so `$text` here already ends with `\n` and appending `'$text\n'` writes a stray blank line after every quarantined record in the `.corrupt` sidecar. Harmless for forensics, but the sidecar then no longer round-trips as one-record-per-line. Append `$text` (or strip the newline and add it back) so the sidecar stays clean JSONL.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment7.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `test/dbg_heal_test.dart` looks like a committed debug leftover**

The `dbg_` filename, five `print` calls (each needing an `avoid_print` ignore), and — most importantly — **zero `expect` assertions** mark this as scaffolding from diagnosing the header-less heal path rather than a regression test. It does still exercise the path (a throw would fail), so either give it real assertions (e.g. expect the healed header, the quarantine sidecar content, and `reopened` entry ids) and rename it into `test/session/`, or drop it — as-is it just adds log noise to the suite.
